for (uint16_t k = 0; k < (uint16_t)((i == 0U) ? numInputNeurons : numHiddenNeurons); k++)
```
Reason:
The explicit cast to `(uint16_t)` ensures that the result of the ternary operation is treated as a `uint16_t`, thus preventing any implicit type conversions and ensuring compliance with MISRA rule 10.4. This enhances type safety and reduces the risk of unexpected behavior in the code.


